\b\lang16393 Tokenization\par
Tokenization\b0  is the first step in a Transformer model's pipeline. It is the process of breaking raw text into smaller units called \b tokens\b0 , which can be words, subwords, characters, or even punctuation marks. Since neural networks cannot directly process text, tokenization converts human language into discrete units that the model can understand.\par
\b Common Tokenization Methods\par
1. Word Tokenization\par
\b0 Plain Text\par
I love Generative AI\par
\f5\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
["I", "love", "Generative", "AI"]\par
Simple but struggles with unseen words.\par
\b 2. Character Tokenization\par
\b0 Plain Text\par
AI\par
\f5\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
["A", "I"]\par
Very flexible but creates long sequences.\par
\b 3. Subword Tokenization (Most Common)\par
\b0 Plain Text\par
unhappiness\par
\f5\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
["un", "happi", "ness"]\par
Used in GPT, BERT, Llama, and most modern LLMs because it balances vocabulary size and flexibility.\par
\b Token IDs\par
\b0 After tokenization, each token is mapped to a numerical ID using a vocabulary lookup table.\par
Plain Text\par
["I", "love", "AI"]\par
\f5\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
[105, 432, 892]\par
These token IDs become the input to the embedding layer.\par
\b Embeddings\par
\b0 Once text has been converted into token IDs, the Transformer must transform these integers into meaningful numerical representations. This is done through \b Embeddings\b0 .\par
An \b Embedding\b0  is a dense vector representation of a token in a high-dimensional space. Instead of representing words as simple numbers, embeddings capture semantic meaning and relationships between words.\par
"King" \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [0.12, -0.45, 0.78, ...]\par
"Queen" \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [0.15, -0.42, 0.81, ...]\par
"Dog" \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [-0.67, 0.12, -0.23, ...]\par
Because "King" and "Queen" are semantically related, their vectors are located close together in the embedding space.\par
\b Why Embeddings are Needed\par
\b0 Token IDs have no meaning by themselves:\par
Plain Text\par
King \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  2456\par
Queen \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  3921\par
Dog \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  789\par
The model cannot infer relationships from these numbers.\par
Embeddings convert them into vectors that encode:\par

\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Meaning\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Context\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Similarity\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Semantic relationships\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\b Embedding Workflow\par
\b0 Plain Text\par
Raw Text\par
\f5\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
Tokenization\par
\f5\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
Token IDs\par
\f5\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
Embedding Lookup\par
\f5\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
Dense Vector Representations\par
Example:\par
Plain Text\par
Sentence:\par
"I love AI"\par
\~\par
Token IDs:\par
[101, 205, 301]\par
\~\par
Embedding Matrix Lookup:\par
[101] \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [0.2, 0.1, -0.4]\par
[205] \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [-0.7, 0.8, 0.2]\par
[301] \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [0.5, -0.1, 0.9]\par
Result:\par
Plain Text\par
[\par
[0.2, 0.1, -0.4],\par
[-0.7, 0.8, 0.2],\par
[0.5, -0.1, 0.9]\par
]\par
These vectors are what the Transformer actually processes.\par
\b Embedding Matrix\par
\b0 Internally, a Transformer maintains a large trainable matrix called the \b Embedding Matrix\b0 .\par
Plain Text\par
Vocabulary Size \'d7 Embedding Dimension\par
Example:\par
Plain Text\par
50,000 \'d7 768\par
where:\par

\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 50,000 = number of tokens in vocabulary\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}768 = vector size of each token\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Plain Text\par
Embedding Matrix\par
\~\par
Token 1 \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [0.1, 0.4, 0.9, ...]\par
Token 2 \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [0.5, 0.3, 0.2, ...]\par
Token 3 \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [0.8, 0.7, 0.1, ...]\par
...\par
Token N \f5\u8594?\f0\lang16393  [...]\par
During training, these embeddings are continuously updated to better capture word meanings.\par
